1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:15,399
All fifty questions from topics 1–5 with model answers — exactly the way the examiner asks. Plus the twelve most important phrases and five mistakes that cost people points. Get ready and answer out loud!

2
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:28,082
How does the task work? The examiner chooses two topics and asks four questions on each. That is eight questions in total, and each good answer gets one point.

3
00:00:28,967 --> 00:00:40,735
You know the topics in advance, but not the questions. So now we will go through all ten questions of each topic. Answer with a full sentence, ideally two, and listen to the tense.

4
00:00:41,633 --> 00:00:45,304
Topic 1: About me. Ten questions.

5
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,057
What is your name?

6
00:00:54,367 --> 00:00:58,142
My name is Oleh Kovalenko. My friends call me Olek.

7
00:00:59,233 --> 00:01:00,242
Where are you from?

8
00:01:07,533 --> 00:01:11,791
I am from Ukraine, from the city of Kharkiv. It is a big city in the east.

9
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:14,403
Where do you live now?

10
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:24,548
Now I live in Kralupy nad Vltavou with my family.

11
00:01:25,633 --> 00:01:27,118
How long have you been in Czechia?

12
00:01:34,433 --> 00:01:38,296
I have been in Czechia for five years. I came in 2021.

13
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,454
What do you do?

14
00:01:47,767 --> 00:01:50,775
I work in a warehouse and in my free time I learn Czech.

15
00:01:51,867 --> 00:01:53,279
What languages do you speak?

16
00:02:00,567 --> 00:02:03,917
I speak Ukrainian, Russian and a little Czech and English.

17
00:02:05,033 --> 00:02:06,232
What kind of person are you?

18
00:02:13,533 --> 00:02:17,345
I think I am calm and friendly. I like helping people.

19
00:02:18,433 --> 00:02:20,483
What did you do before you came to Czechia?

20
00:02:27,767 --> 00:02:30,339
In Ukraine I worked as a shop assistant.

21
00:02:31,433 --> 00:02:32,792
Why did you come to Czechia?

22
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:43,283
I came because of work and because my relatives live here.

23
00:02:44,367 --> 00:02:46,480
What would you like to do in five years?

24
00:02:53,767 --> 00:02:57,093
In five years I would like to have a better job and speak Czech well.

25
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:02,106
Topic 2: Family. Ten questions.

26
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:04,040
How many people are there in your family?

27
00:03:11,333 --> 00:03:15,098
There are four of us: my wife, two sons and me.

28
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:17,665
Do you have any brothers or sisters?

29
00:03:24,967 --> 00:03:29,805
Yes, I have one brother. He is three years older and lives in Ukraine.

30
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:32,548
Where do your parents live?

31
00:03:39,833 --> 00:03:42,748
My parents live in Ukraine in a small town by a river.

32
00:03:43,833 --> 00:03:46,428
What does your husband or wife do?

33
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:56,698
My wife works in a hospital as a nurse.

34
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,226
How old are your children?

35
00:04:06,533 --> 00:04:10,705
My son is nine and my daughter is five. My son is in the third year at school.

36
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,455
What do you like doing as a family?

37
00:04:20,767 --> 00:04:23,976
As a family we like going for walks and at the weekend we play games.

38
00:04:25,067 --> 00:04:26,704
How often do you call your parents?

39
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,140
I call my parents almost every evening when they are at home.

40
00:04:38,233 --> 00:04:40,481
When did you last see your parents?

41
00:04:47,767 --> 00:04:51,650
I last saw my parents last summer when they came to visit.

42
00:04:52,733 --> 00:04:55,319
How did you celebrate the last birthday in your family?

43
00:05:02,633 --> 00:05:06,478
Last month we had a party at home for our son with a cake and friends.

44
00:05:07,567 --> 00:05:09,687
Where will you go with your family next time?

45
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,730
Next summer we will go to the sea in Croatia with the family.

46
00:05:20,833 --> 00:05:24,967
Topic 3: Friends. Ten questions.

47
00:05:25,467 --> 00:05:27,007
Do you have friends in the Czech Republic?

48
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:38,385
Yes, I have several friends here. I know some of them from work.

49
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:41,602
How often do you meet your friends?

50
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:52,503
I meet my friends about once a week, usually on Saturday.

51
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:55,918
What does your best friend look like?

52
00:06:03,233 --> 00:06:07,883
My best friend is tall, has short black hair and wears glasses.

53
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,583
What is your best friend like?

54
00:06:17,867 --> 00:06:20,871
He's cheerful and always helps when I have a problem.

55
00:06:21,967 --> 00:06:23,265
What do you do with your friends?

56
00:06:30,567 --> 00:06:34,151
We go to a café, play football or have a barbecue.

57
00:06:35,267 --> 00:06:37,594
Where did you meet your best friend?

58
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:48,202
I met my best friend at work three years ago.

59
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:52,291
When did you last visit a friend and why?

60
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:03,466
Last Sunday I visited a friend because it was his birthday.

61
00:07:04,567 --> 00:07:05,969
Do you have Czech friends?

62
00:07:13,267 --> 00:07:17,282
I have one Czech friend. She helps me with Czech.

63
00:07:18,367 --> 00:07:20,557
What will you do with your friends at the weekend?

64
00:07:27,867 --> 00:07:30,355
At the weekend my friends and I will go on a trip to Prague.

65
00:07:31,467 --> 00:07:33,430
Why are friends important?

66
00:07:40,733 --> 00:07:44,212
Friends are important because I can talk to them about everything.

67
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:49,365
Topic 4: Housing. Ten questions.

68
00:07:49,867 --> 00:07:51,511
Do you live in a flat or a house?

69
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:01,074
I live in a flat in a prefab block on the third floor.

70
00:08:02,167 --> 00:08:03,681
How big is your flat?

71
00:08:10,967 --> 00:08:14,615
Our flat is a 2+1. It has two rooms and a kitchen.

72
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:17,086
How much do you pay in rent?

73
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:27,695
We pay twelve thousand crowns a month in rent, including utilities.

74
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:30,617
What do you have in your living room?

75
00:08:37,933 --> 00:08:42,218
In the living room we have a sofa, a table, a TV and a big wardrobe.

76
00:08:43,333 --> 00:08:46,258
What furniture does everyone need and why?

77
00:08:53,567 --> 00:08:56,751
Everyone needs a bed because they have to sleep well.

78
00:08:57,867 --> 00:08:59,304
Do you like your flat?

79
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:10,299
Yes, I like it because it's bright and there's a park nearby.

80
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:13,472
What was your home like when you were a child?

81
00:09:20,767 --> 00:09:23,870
As a child I lived with my parents in a small house with a garden.

82
00:09:24,967 --> 00:09:27,154
When did you last move house?

83
00:09:34,467 --> 00:09:37,514
I last moved two years ago, to a bigger flat.

84
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,341
What would you like to change in your flat?

85
00:09:47,633 --> 00:09:50,022
I'd like a new kitchen and a bigger bathroom.

86
00:09:51,133 --> 00:09:53,523
What kind of home would you like in ten years?

87
00:10:00,833 --> 00:10:03,598
In ten years I'd like my own house with a garden.

88
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:08,552
Topic 5: My town. Ten questions.

89
00:10:09,067 --> 00:10:10,559
Which town do you live in?

90
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:21,860
I live in Kralupy nad Vltavou. It's a small town near Prague.

91
00:10:22,967 --> 00:10:25,065
Is your town big or small?

92
00:10:32,367 --> 00:10:35,837
My town is small, it has about eighteen thousand inhabitants.

93
00:10:36,933 --> 00:10:39,012
What is interesting in your town?

94
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:49,388
The Vltava river and a nice park by the station are interesting.

95
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:52,233
Where do you like going most in town?

96
00:10:59,533 --> 00:11:02,306
I like going to the park and walking by the river most.

97
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:05,544
How do you get to work in town?

98
00:11:12,833 --> 00:11:16,481
I go to work by bus, the journey takes fifteen minutes.

99
00:11:17,567 --> 00:11:19,083
What is missing in your town?

100
00:11:26,367 --> 00:11:28,744
There's no cinema and not enough playgrounds for children.

101
00:11:29,833 --> 00:11:32,607
What was your town like when you arrived?

102
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:43,313
When I arrived, the town was quiet and I didn't know anyone.

103
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:46,680
What did you do in town last Saturday?

104
00:11:53,967 --> 00:11:57,533
Last Saturday I went to the market on the square and bought vegetables.

105
00:11:58,633 --> 00:12:00,897
Will you live in this town in the future too?

106
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:12,667
Yes, I think I'll live here in the future too, because I like it here.

107
00:12:13,767 --> 00:12:16,400
What would you recommend to a tourist in your town?

108
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:26,904
I'd recommend a walk along the river and a visit to the church.

109
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:32,707
Now the twelve most important phrases. Listen and repeat out loud.

110
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,253
My name is Oleh Kovalenko.

111
00:12:38,467 --> 00:12:40,767
I am from Ukraine, from Kharkiv.

112
00:12:43,967 --> 00:12:46,000
I live in Kralupy nad Vltavou.

113
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:50,700
I have been in Czechia for five years.

114
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:55,100
I work in a warehouse.

115
00:12:58,300 --> 00:13:00,094
I have a wife and two sons.

116
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:05,631
In my free time I like going for walks.

117
00:13:08,833 --> 00:13:11,396
I like the flat because it is bright.

118
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,533
Last Saturday I was at the market.

119
00:13:19,733 --> 00:13:21,500
Next summer we will go to the sea.

120
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:26,967
In five years I would like to have a better job.

121
00:13:30,167 --> 00:13:32,367
I think I am calm and friendly.

122
00:13:35,567 --> 00:13:38,625
Five typical mistakes that cost people points.

123
00:13:41,833 --> 00:13:48,059
Correct: Bydlím v Kralupech nad Vltavou. Answer with a full sentence, not one word.

124
00:13:51,767 --> 00:13:57,376
Correct: Jsem z Ukrajiny. After the preposition z we use the 2nd case: z Ukrajiny, z Kyjeva.

125
00:14:01,067 --> 00:14:08,000
Correct: Bydlím v Praze. After the preposition v we use the 6th case: v Praze, v Brně.

126
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:17,731
Correct: Je mi čtyřicet let. This is how we say age: je mi … let.

127
00:14:21,433 --> 00:14:29,186
Correct: Rodiče jsem naposledy viděl loni v létě. The question is in the past tense, so the answer must be too.

128
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:52,095
Summary. First: answer with a full sentence, ideally two. Second: listen to the tense of the question and answer in the same tense. Third: watch the cases — z Ukrajiny, v Praze. And fourth: be specific — numbers, places, names.

129
00:14:53,300 --> 00:15:02,544
